## Windows

### GtkApplicationWindow

Handle `onCloseRequest` and return `true` to veto GTK's native close so React state unmounts the window.

```tsx
<GtkApplicationWindow
    title="App"
    defaultWidth={800}
    defaultHeight={600}
    onCloseRequest={() => {
        quit();
        return true;
    }}
>
    <Content />
</GtkApplicationWindow>
```

Custom titlebar:
```tsx
<GtkApplicationWindow ... titlebar={<GtkHeaderBar />}>
    <Content />
</GtkApplicationWindow>
```

